// The tie whose question is the SHAPE — the arm that fires when the medium
// will not claim more than it read. `scaled()` and `stepped()` are both Pure,
// so no row separates them; but the constant read folds literals, arithmetic
// and unary operators and STOPS at a branch, so it cannot say what either
// one denotes. The honest answer is then the weaker, true one — these are
// different structures — never a guess that they agree.
//
// That refusal is the whole point of gating this arm: DivName is reported
// only where every survivor's value was actually read, so a tie can never be
// called a naming question on the strength of an unread body.
//
// A PROJECTION fixture (it carries an authored hole, so it is never an
// executable); the gate reads its Propose facet.

fn scaled() -> Int with Pure = if 2 > 1 { 40 } else { 4 }

fn stepped() -> Int with Pure = if 3 > 1 { 40 } else { 5 }

fn total() -> Int with Pure = ??

fn main() = total()
